id: pm-ycv2cz
title: "GH-1232: Normalize policy authoring ids with actionable mismatch recovery"
description: A positional policy id must populate an omitted definition.id; a self-contained definition must work without a second id; conflicting ids must fail before durable writes with actionable guidance.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-11T06:19:08.219Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-11T07:57:47.712Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-11T06:58:58.400Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-11T06:58:58.400Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: SDK CLI and MCP support either id source and identical ids; mismatch and malformed id fail atomically; a refusal gives enough information to repair the invocation.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make governance contracts independently understandable and executable across all transports
value: Reduce agent retry cost while preserving declared workspace guarantees
parent: pm-f05lsg
repro_steps: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1232"
resolution: "Normalize policy ids once in the SDK from either operand or definition, preserve atomic mismatch rejection and align CLI/MCP schema 4.19."
expected_result: Either single id source succeeds; conflicting ids refuse without registry or history writes.
actual_result: "Real SDK/CLI/MCP tests pass for both sources, normalized idempotence and immutable mismatch refusal; generated contracts and SDK surface agree."
